---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, ANALYTICS } from '../site.config';

const title = 'Privacy Policy';
const description = `How ${SITE.name} handles data: what is collected, what is not, cookies, analytics, and your rights.`;
const updated = '2026-08-18';
const effective = 'August 18, 2026';

const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: `Privacy Policy — ${SITE.name}`,
    url: new URL('/privacy/', SITE.url).href,
    dateModified: updated,
  },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} updated={updated} schema={schema} ogType="article">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">Effective {effective}.</p>

    <p>
      {SITE.name} ("we", "the site") is an independent fan project published at{' '}
      <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url.replace('https://', '')}</a>, and is the index for every wiki in
      the Hunt Games network. This policy covers this index page only. Each game wiki under
      hunt-games.com is built and deployed separately and may publish its own privacy policy at its
      own subdomain — check the site you're on if you followed a link from here.
    </p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a set of static pages. There are no accounts, no logins, no comments, and no
      newsletter. We do not ask you for personal information anywhere on this index.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <h3>Information you give us</h3>
    <p>
      None, unless you choose to email us. If you do, we receive whatever you put in the message and
      keep it only as long as needed to reply.
    </p>

    <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
    <p>
      Our hosting provider processes standard server and network request data — IP address, browser
      user-agent, requested URL, timestamp — as an ordinary part of delivering the page to you and
      protecting the service from abuse. We do not use these logs to build profiles of individuals.
    </p>
    {
      ANALYTICS.gaMeasurementId ? (
        <Fragment>
          <h3>Analytics</h3>
          <p>
            We use Google Analytics to understand which entries in the index get used. It sets
            cookies and reports aggregate usage — pages viewed, approximate region, device type,
            referring site. We have no interest in identifying individual visitors and do not attempt
            to. Google's handling of this data is governed by the{' '}
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener nofollow">
              Google Privacy Policy
            </a>
            . You can opt out with the{' '}
            <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener nofollow">
              Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on
            </a>
            , or by blocking the script in your browser or an extension.
          </p>
        </Fragment>
      ) : (
        <Fragment>
          <h3>Analytics</h3>
          <p>
            This index currently runs no analytics or tracking scripts. If that changes, this policy
            will be updated before the change goes live, and the effective date at the top will move.
          </p>
        </Fragment>
      )
    }

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no cookies of its own.{' '}
      {
        ANALYTICS.gaMeasurementId
          ? 'The analytics provider described above sets its own cookies; blocking them does not affect anything on this site.'
          : 'With no analytics running, a visit should leave no cookies at all.'
      }{' '}
      Nothing on the site depends on cookies to function.
    </p>

    <h2>Outbound links</h2>
    <p>
      Every card in the index links out to a separate site — either another Hunt Games wiki on its
      own subdomain, or (rarely) an external reference. Once you follow a link you're on that site's
      property and its own privacy policy applies. We don't control what those sites collect, and
      following a link from here doesn't send them any information about you beyond the ordinary
      referrer your browser already sends on any click.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect information from
      them. If you believe a child has sent us personal information by email, contact us and we will
      delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live — including under the GDPR in the EU/UK and the CCPA in California
      — you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or restrict processing of your personal
      data, and to object to it. Because this site holds essentially none, most such requests are
      satisfied by explaining that there is nothing to return. To exercise any of these rights, or to
      ask what we hold, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Data retention and security</h2>
    <p>
      We do not maintain a database of visitors. Server logs are retained by the hosting provider
      under their own schedule. The site is served over HTTPS.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes materially, the effective date above changes with it. Continuing to use
      the site after an update means you accept the revised policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="small muted">
      This policy describes our actual practices in plain language. It is not legal advice.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
